  "definitions": {
    "jet_anomaly": "Energy of the raw change in the horizontally averaged current from its own initial profile, including any uniform momentum drift; distinct from energy already present in the imposed shear. The cosine-shape diagnostic separately removes depth-mean change.",
    "ky0_eddy_fraction": "Eky0_eddy/Eeddy, with horizontally uniform mean energy removed from both numerator and denominator. Full Eky0 and Ehorizontal_mean remain separate.",
    "native_3d": "Native advection of the full field minus native advection evaluated on the replicated y mean; scheme-dependent, not identical to a continuum Reynolds covariance.",
    "jet_spacing": "Cosine least-squares diagnostic of the changed depth profile on the bounded vertical interval. 2H/n is a descriptive wavelength, not a periodic-box spectrum or an eigenmode prediction.",
    "closure": "Native sampled endpoint tendencies, including the actual closure term; any mismatch remains reported. No post-hoc term repairs the budget.",
    "pressure": "The horizontal mean of the native gradient of the last projection pressure is a periodicity check; it vanishes for any periodic pressure and is not an instantaneous pointwise pressure solve.",
